      "title": "Tennessee halts plan to execute woman for first time in 200 years",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/30/tennessee-execution-halted-christa-pike",
      "description": "<p>State governor and supreme court earlier refused calls for clemency for Christa Pike, who was convicted of murder</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tennessee\">Tennessee</a>’s first execution of a woman in 200 years was halted by a court on Wednesday morning an hour before it was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/28/tennessee-woman-execution-christa-pike\">set to take place</a>.</p><p>The state governor and the supreme court had earlier refused calls for clemency in the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/sep/05/christa-pike-death-row-clemency-petition\">case of Christa Pike</a>, who was convicted of murder 30 years ago.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/30/tennessee-execution-halted-christa-pike\">Continue reading...</a>",
